\[
\begin{cases}
x'(t) = 4y(t) \\[5pt]
y'(t) = -4x(t),
\end{cases}
\qquad \begin{bmatrix} x(1) \\ y(1) \end{bmatrix} =  \begin{bmatrix} 0 \\ 3  \end{bmatrix}
\]
Find the solution to the initial value problem above.</p>
<p><em>Hint: $e^{At} = \begin{bmatrix} \cos(4t) & \sin(4t) \\ -\sin(4t) & \cos(4t) \end{bmatrix},$ where $A = \begin{bmatrix} 0 & 4 \\ -4 & 0 \end{bmatrix}.$</em>
